        "original_id": "40c48587-3bc2-54f2-944c-e0cda57e6bca",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Marinelli Glacier, Alberto de Agostini National Park, Isla Grande de Tierra del Fuego, South America, Strait of Magellan, Tierra del Fuego, Chile\n- Systems: Marinelli Creek\n- Concepts: tidewater glacier, island, watercourse, headwaters, glacier melt\n\nFacts:\n- Isla Grande de Tierra del Fuego, also called Tierra del Fuego, was formerly known as Isla de Xativa.\n- Tierra del Fuego literally means \"Land of the Fire.\"\n- Isla Grande de Tierra del Fuego is an island near the southern tip of South America and is separated from South America by the Strait of Magellan.\n- Marinelli Glacier is a tidewater glacier in Alberto de Agostini National Park on Isla Grande de Tierra del Fuego.\n- Marinelli Creek is a watercourse in Tierra del Fuego, Chile.\n- The headwaters of Marinelli Creek emerge from the melting of Marinelli Glacier.",
